# Ionos SMTP Configuration Options

# Option 1: Standard STARTTLS (Port 587)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.ionos.co.uk
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=info@aspirefootballgroup.co.uk
SMTP_PASS=your-ionos-password

# Option 2: SSL (Port 465)
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.ionos.co.uk
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=info@aspirefootballgroup.co.uk
# SMTP_PASS=your-ionos-password

# Option 3: Alternative Ionos hostnames to try
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.1and1.co.uk
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=info@aspirefootballgroup.co.uk
# SMTP_PASS=your-ionos-password

# Option 4: If above don't work, try:
# SMTP_HOST=auth.smtp.1and1.co.uk
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=info@aspirefootballgroup.co.uk
# SMTP_PASS=your-ionos-password

# Notes for Ionos:
# 1. Make sure SMTP is enabled in your Ionos email settings
# 2. Try different hostnames if one doesn't work
# 3. Check if your domain uses 1and1 or ionos servers
# 4. Ensure no firewall blocking outbound SMTP ports